Student Conduct and Academic Integrity Policy

This sample policy document outlines expectations for academic honesty, respectful conduct, disciplinary review, and appeal rights. It is included as a public-style policy document for the local RAG lab corpus. The policy applies to classroom activity, online learning, internships, university housing, events, and official digital platforms.

Academic integrity requires students to submit their own work, cite sources accurately, and follow assessment instructions. Prohibited behavior includes plagiarism, unauthorized collaboration, contract cheating, fabrication of data, impersonation, and use of unauthorized materials during examinations.

Students are expected to treat other members of the university community with respect. Harassment, threats, discrimination, retaliation, property damage, and disruption of university activities may be reviewed under the conduct process. Reports may be submitted by students, employees, visitors, or campus partners.

When a report is received, the conduct office may conduct an initial review, gather information, and notify the student of alleged violations. Students may respond to allegations, provide evidence, identify witnesses, and bring a support person when permitted by procedure.

Sanctions may include warning, educational assignments, probation, restitution, suspension, expulsion, transcript notation, or restrictions on access to facilities and activities. Sanctions are selected based on severity, prior history, impact, and the need to protect the community.

Appeals must be filed by the stated deadline and must identify procedural error, new information, disproportionate sanction, or conflict of interest. The appeal officer may affirm, modify, or return the matter for further review.

